sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Campaign Service
    participant CDB as Campaign DB
    participant O as Campaign Outbox Relay
    participant N as NATS JetStream
    participant D as Delivery Orchestration
    participant DDB as Delivery DB
    participant A as Audience/Consent APIs
    participant W as Delivery Worker
    participant S as SMTP Transport
    participant X as Analytics

    C->>CDB: Commit scheduled campaign + outbox event
    O->>CDB: Lease unpublished outbox rows
    O->>N: Publish campaign.scheduled.v1 with stable event ID
    N-->>O: Durable publish acknowledgement
    O->>CDB: Mark outbox event published
    N->>D: Deliver event at least once
    D->>DDB: Deduplicate in inbox and persist delivery plan/outbox
    D->>A: Request scoped eligible audience snapshot
    A-->>D: Immutable snapshot reference + version
    D->>DDB: Persist bounded jobs and tenant/domain policy
    D->>N: Publish delivery.requested.v1
    N->>W: Deliver job reference (may be duplicated)
    W->>DDB: Claim lease and deduplicate
    W->>A: Verify current consent/suppression decision
    A-->>W: Eligible/blocked decision
    W->>S: Submit immutable rendered message
    S-->>W: SMTP reply and classified result
    W->>DDB: Persist attempt/result and outbox event
    W->>N: Acknowledge only after durable result
    N->>X: Publish delivery outcome
    X->>X: Deduplicate and aggregate event

    Note over W,S: Exactly-once external SMTP delivery is not guaranteed. Uncertain replies require reconciliation, not blind resend.

